     "SimHamiltonian"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "f646a789-10be-5a42-b828-1429707011d7"],
     ". It defines the field strength for which the hamiltonian is calculated \
defined in Tesla."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"420cd4ec-d434-974e-8309-045f87fee0f4"]},
   {Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "1db6132a-c3a4-924c-9002-6413be60034f"], 
    ButtonBox["SimNucleus",
     BaseStyle->"Link",
     ButtonData->"paclet:QMRITools/ref/SimNucleus"], "\"\<1H\>\"", Cell[
    TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      ButtonBox["SimNucleus",
       BaseStyle->"Link",
       ButtonData->"paclet:QMRITools/ref/SimNucleus"]], "InlineFormula",
      ExpressionUUID->"747860ee-e59c-d841-aeb0-e98504d7e8e8"],
     " is an option for ",
     Cell[BoxData[
     "SimHamiltonian"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "7e36aebf-6771-7c42-8bf1-48649e38dbab"],
     ". It defines the nucleus for which to simulate the spectra."
